Multiplying the first equation by 2 and the second equation by 4, we get:
\begin{align*}
8u - 10v &= 46 \\
8u + 16v &= -32
\end{align*}
Subtracting the second equation from the first equation, we get:
\begin{align*}
-26v &= 78 \\
v &= -3
\end{align*}
Substituting $v = -3$ into the first equation, we get:
\begin{align*}
4u - 5(-3) &= 23 \\
4u + 15 &= 23 \\
4u &= 8 \\
u &= 2
\end{align*}
